{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them","id":368430,"title":"Crossroads, I missed them","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-13T02:08:24-08:00","id":368430,"title":"Crossroads, I missed them","content":"Well, that's it.<br /> <br /> I just finished reading the DtD core section (it's pending only Seattle and rules revisions so far), and just couldn't find any reference to a well know flavor in most demon folklore (mainly dealing with pacts, I think): <b>the crossroads</b>,<br /> <br /> An Embed, Exploit or an innate hability? I don't know... but I miss it in some way...<br /> <br /> Anybody else? If so, how would you implement it?<br /> <br /> My take would be somekind of teleport/summoning Exploit involving &quot;disrupting/hacking&quot; occult matrices &quot;circuits/flux&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":646,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","user":"mabafu","date":". 01-13-2015, 05:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T02:24:16-08:00","id":368453,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/98/Tha_Crossroads.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>?<br /> <br /> More seriously, you mean like a Robert Johnson sort of thing? Pacts, I think, cover that pretty well. If you wanted a special thing, I might have an Embed where you can use it at a crossroads and know if someone for, say, Primum=Weeks went there to sell their soul. While useless by itself, it could have some use for a talented with Urban Legends sort of Demon.<br /> <br /> I mean, no Embed or Exploit would be required, and I would certainly be amused by a PC who used that as a means to get souls, but if you wanted a mechanic I would go with that. True or not it is something a Demon can exploit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T03:06:21-08:00","id":368490,"title":"","content":"Four roads coming together as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T06:37:21-08:00","id":368562,"title":"","content":"As flavorful as meeting a demon at a crossroads is, I don't feel like that particular bit of folklore fits the Unchained. You could easily enough work that into an <a href=\"https://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/59019/World-of-Darkness-Inferno?term=world+of+darkness+inferno\" target=\"_blank\">Infernal demon's</a>...whatever those things are called. Summoning rites? Templates?<br /> <br /> The big problem is that having a reliable way to summon a demon is something you can use to exploit them. Not to mention that by necessity you'd be revealing yourself to a mortal, which is a harsh Compromise by itself. Even if you showed up in demon form only (to keep your Covers secure) I wouldn't risk it, especially with any amount of regularity.<br /> <br /> I don't like being the guy who says &quot;You shouldn't do this&quot;, but remember that Demon is a game about Techngnostic Espionage, and including crossroads as a thing would be weird.<br /> <br /> This isn't as relevant, but I also never heard about demons at crossroads specifically until I started watching Supernatural. I don't think it's important to the lore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T07:34:07-08:00","id":368601,"title":"","content":"Since my last post was such a negative Nancy, &quot;Stop Having Fun, Guys&quot; kind of post, I'll make this one constructive. I'd implement this as a Merit of some sort.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Crossroad Pact-Making (* to *****</u></b><u>+</u><b><u>)</u></b><br /> Unchained are not slaves to the legends of demons any more than they are to the God-Machine itself. However, that doesn't mean that they are incapable or unwilling to exploit some of the tales. In this case, the legends of pacts with demons made at crossroads.<br /> <b>Effect: </b>Each dot in this Merit gives an Unchained purview over another specific intersection of at least two roads. The Unchained also describes a common ritual that can be performed at each intersection. When a character performs the ritual at one of the Demon's intersections, the Demon is immediately made aware that <i>someone</i> is trying to contact them. She does not receive any information about the summoner unless she has some sort of remote surveillance at the site, nor does she obtain a way to quickly travel to the intersection. She must drive, fly, or use some sort of Embed or Exploit to get there (or possibly bring the summoner to them, perhaps using the Summon Exploit).<br /> The Merit does not provide any sort of protection from Compromise checks made if the demon reveals herself to the summoner. If a pact is made at one of the locations, the Willpower point cost of the pact is reduced by one. The Willpower dot sacrifice for Soul Pacts cannot be eliminated, however.<br /> <br /> I hope this gives you something like what you're looking for. I figured simply having an associated intersection per crossroad wouldn't be worth a Merit point, so I included the Willpower discount. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:13:35-08:00","id":368624,"title":"","content":"Actually, the crossroads is one of the very first references to the Unchained (though arguably as it could admittedly fit a denizen of the Inferno also) in the setting, as it appeared on page 75-78 of Midnight Roads. (The Dark Man sounds like a facade to me!) I think this is the primary reason crossroads aren't <i>directly</i> referenced in Demon the Descent, as they're something special you'd come to in a traveling chronicle. (There are a few more potential God-Machine related hooks here too, gremlins and an old man on the lam from <i>something</i>.)<br /> <br /> That said: They do hint heavily at these things. There are many means with which an Unchained can get around and construct a phoney ritual to summon them. They start an urban legend with the help of their exploits and embeds, make sure it spreads like a meme. Then, using their talents for investigation, they simply track whom might be looking into the legend they've begun, track potentials, because appearing in a gout of flame at the stroke of midnight is an easy feat for one of the Unchained; so long as they know where to be. Bonus: Mortals that believe they're summoning something from the beyond to make a deal allow the demon to make use of their powers more freely and openly before them without risking compromise - after all, they're a demon in the mortal's mind here.<br /> <br /> As a result, I think the whole crossroads demon might just be a nice story a demon started a while back, nobody remembers who, but everybody loves to take that for a ride and make some easy and dramatic deals.<br /> <br /> One of my players did this very thing taking a page from Hellraiser. She took a rubik's cube and turned it into 'The Nightmare Box'. A gadget which allowed her to facilitate her demonic pacts in a very deliberate and occult way. As an exploited gadget it took on an arcane style and when it was solved, it became increasingly complicated and impossible and demanded to be solved again and again until, finally, the person completes it and opens it. When they do this, they were inflicted with stigmata, but only for a short period. The powers, merits and second-sight into the God-Machine that came with this stigmata would evaporate after 3 days. Since she always took the cube from the claimant after making the deal and always used Tag and Release to keep track of it, she had an easy way to appear. She'd follow the device wherever it might go in her spare hours and when she saw someone had solved it - largely because they began to see how the world really was - she'd scoop them up and announce herself as some otherworldly, hellish entity that would reward them with a bargain. Sometimes she was a god, an alien, or even just a demon.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I believe, a demon might be able to create a &quot;ritual of the crossroads&quot;. Get a cover working a bar or diner on a crossroads and use Special Message on several of the songs that play over the radio. Have the message trigger on criteria such as &quot;a below average guitar player&quot; and have the message promise &quot;their heart's desire given in a devil's deal&quot;. Then simply watch the crossroads at midnight and use some other trick to make for a heart stopping appearance when one of the fish bites. Using other embeds, like Earworm.<br /> <br /> Or do the whole thing the easy way with Urban Legend from Flowers of Hell. It's an exploit that literally gives you control over a story like that, making the principal characters facades you can use when complete, in this case the &quot;Crossroads Demon&quot; (or 'The Dark Man' perhaps?) would become a facade you can wear when someone actively pursues the story. If you lie in wait and use Teleport or use Urban Fluidity, you can get there quick and in a blur or instant; 'summoned'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","user":"DesolateDolly","date":". 01-13-2015, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:34:46-08:00","id":368650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DesolateDolly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them?p=368624#post368624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the crossroads is one of the very first references to the Unchained (though arguably as it could admittedly fit a denizen of the Inferno also) in the setting, as it appeared on page 75-78 of Midnight Roads. (The Dark Man sounds like a facade to me!)</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're referring to this\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD Core p23, &quot;Demons, Demons, Demons.&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, finally, Demon: The Descent demons. A few appear in Promethean: The Created and its line. One cameos in World of Darkness: Midnight Roads.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026then I can say with some certainty that the Dark Man isn't the definite cameo in question.<br /> <br /> That's Mister Blue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD: Midnight Roads, p39, &quot;Mister Blue.&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A well-dressed man in a blue suit, carrying a neat briefcase and a brand-new duffle. His skin is pale but healthy, and he\u2019s somehow tamed long, blond curls into a ponytail. Mister Blue\u2019s car broke down, and he\u2019d be very grateful if someone could give him a lift. Just to a gas station or something, he doesn\u2019t want to be trouble. He\u2019ll even pay\u2026 how\u2019s a hundred bucks sound? Oh, is that a lot?<br /> <br /> He\u2019s not used to traveling the roads, you know. You must see all sorts of things. Say, what about that last town you visited? He\u2019s heard a lot of things about that town. He\u2019s not sure he\u2019d want to go there. Still, not his to judge.<br /> <br /> Once Mister Blue\u2019s in the car, he peppers the driver and passengers with questions, mostly about the last place they were. The drive to whatever nearby destination you agreed on seems interminable. Still, he\u2019s as good as his word, paying you off in crisp new bills as soon as you arrive. He makes a call, then a tow truck arrives to take him back the way he came.<br /> <br /> You won\u2019t hear anything more about Mister Blue for a few days. If you told him good things about the town, you\u2019ll see a news story about something surprising and wonderful; an oil strike, perhaps, or an anonymous donor leaving the city an enormous donation. If you filled him in on the town\u2019s sins and dirty dealings, though, you\u2019ll hear about a horrible fire or other disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:53:51-08:00","id":368706,"title":"","content":"Thanks all you guys for the input. Baron's approach is very subtle, I liked it. <br /> <br /> By no means I suggested some kind of &quot;coercive&quot; ritual that could bring the demon against his will to the crossroads site. That said, I diagree it don't fits Unchained... fitting in this case is a matter of twisting &quot;folklore&quot; (lie) to &quot;factual game mechanics&quot; (true), it's done all the time over all main splats... including DtD.<br /> <br /> The Urban Legend Exploit, seems exactly what I've missed... and it sounds pretty generic to encompass a bunch of other &quot;folklores&quot;, Thanks for the reference Dolly, I don't know any suplements yet!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:33:47-08:00","id":368974,"title":"","content":"Allow me to stop and ask a question: why do you need a mechanic for a set piece? Particularly a prominent one in today's world?<br /> <br /> If you want to ensure people make deals at a crossroads, use Summon and wait. But as for crossroads, it just falls on you or the storyteller to employ them in the actions of characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T14:58:50-08:00","id":368990,"title":"","content":"Sometimes road systems are Infrastructure. Which might give demons reasons to show up at (and avoid) certain areas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:06:10-08:00","id":369172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them?p=368974#post368974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to stop and ask a question: why do you need a mechanic for a set piece? Particularly a prominent one in today's world?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't need it. I just missed it,as it's frequently found in many &quot;tales&quot; about &quot;demon pacts&quot;. Just a flavor, that could have some kind of game mechanic. But I agree, with you and others that followed this line of reasoning, it can be easily obtained thematically and indirectly (regarding the mechanics).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them?p=368990#post368990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes road systems are Infrastructure. Which might give demons reasons to show up at (and avoid) certain areas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup... infrastructre. I also thought about it, I just could not find anything appropriate to link it with pacts. I can figure out roads as conduits of some sort, and it's interceptions having some occult (matrix) relevance. But how to co-relate it with demon pacts? Using that conduits like kueijin used &quot;ley lines&quot; of cWoD would be an approach... but it would cover the &quot;traveling&quot; mood... the pact stuff, just scapes me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/646-mabafu","name":"mabafu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar646_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T17:59:40-08:00","id":369231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mabafu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them?p=369172#post369172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup... infrastructre. I also thought about it, I just could not find anything appropriate to link it with pacts. I can figure out roads as conduits of some sort, and it's interceptions having some occult (matrix) relevance. But how to co-relate it with demon pacts? Using that conduits like kueijin used &amp;quot;ley lines&amp;quot; of cWoD would be an approach... but it would cover the &amp;quot;traveling&amp;quot; mood... the pact stuff, just scapes me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suborned Infrastructure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T23:46:09-08:00","id":369507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/368430-crossroads-i-missed-them?p=368650#post368650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're referring to this\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026then I can say with some certainty that the Dark Man isn't the definite cameo in question.<br /> <br /> That's Mister Blue.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I completely missed Mister Blue, Satchel. I'd say you're right there that he is probably the cameo. Though Old Man Meier always struck me as a decent candidate for being a Demon as he is hiding from someone or something and it even implies this might be angelic in nature (though they use more traditional imagery in their suggestion.) Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3036-desolatedolly","name":"DesolateDolly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3036_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join 